### Orvexa API v1 — journey step 06: conversations
### The interaction created in step 04 auto-opened (or joined) the customer's
### open chat conversation. Inspect it, work the timeline, assign, and — when
### the whole journey is done — close it (terminal).

@ORVEXA_URL = {{$processEnv ORVEXA_URL}}
@ORVEXA_KEY = {{$processEnv ORVEXA_KEY}}

### List open conversations → 200 (status ∈ open|closed)
# @name listOpenConversations
GET {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/conversations?status=open&limit=25
X-API-Key: {{ORVEXA_KEY}}

###

### Get the first open conversation
# (replace with a concrete id after the first run — REST Client resolves the
#  JSONPath once listOpenConversations has returned data)
# @name getConversation
GET {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/conversations/{{listOpenConversations.response.body.$.data[0].id}}
X-API-Key: {{ORVEXA_KEY}}

###

### Interaction timeline of the conversation → 200
# records serialize with the documented snake_case keys (id/status/…) —
#   see docs/api-clients.md → “Live wire contract notes”
# @name conversationTimeline
GET {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/conversations/{{listOpenConversations.response.body.$.data[0].id}}/interactions
X-API-Key: {{ORVEXA_KEY}}

###

### Assign agent + queue → 200 (either id alone is fine)
# @name assignConversation
POST {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/conversations/{{listOpenConversations.response.body.$.data[0].id}}/assign
X-API-Key: {{ORVEXA_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "agent_id": "{{registerAgent.response.body.$.data.id}}",
  "queue_id": "{{createQueue.response.body.$.data.id}}"
}

###

### Close the conversation → 200 (TERMINAL — run deliberately, last)
# @name closeConversation
POST {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/conversations/{{listOpenConversations.response.body.$.data[0].id}}/close
X-API-Key: {{ORVEXA_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "resolved"
}
